\subsection{Reduced physical-MSE optimization}
\label{sec:adaptation-reduced-mse-envelope}
For $\omega\gg\omega_R$, the reconstruction error in
\eqref{eq:adapt-G-error} is approximately $4(\omega_R/\omega)^4$.
Writing
$m_{-4}=(2\pi)^{-1}\int\omega^{-4}S_\eta^{(2)}(\omega)\,d\omega$,
the reduced physical objective and minimizer are
\begin{align}
J_{\rm red}(\omega_R)&\simeq
\frac{3q_{\rm eff}}{2\omega_R^3}+4m_{-4}\omega_R^4,
\label{eq:adapt-reduced-physical-mse}\\
(\omega_R^\star)^7&=\frac{9q_{\rm eff}}{32m_{-4}}.
\label{eq:adapt-reduced-mse-pole}
\end{align}
The first term is integration drift; the second is physical wave distortion.
Substitution into \eqref{eq:adapt-omegaR} gives
\begin{equation}
r_S^\star=\left(\frac{32}{9}\right)^{3/7}
q_{\rm eff}^{1/14}m_{-4}^{3/7}T_S^{-1/2}.
\label{eq:adapt-reduced-mse-rs}
\end{equation}
For a fixed-shape dilation of the physical acceleration spectrum,
\begin{equation}
m_{-4}=A\widehat\sigma_{a,B}^2\tau^8,
\qquad C_J=(32A/9)^{3/7},
\label{eq:adapt-mminus4-similarity}
\end{equation}
where dimensionless $A$ includes the normalized spectral shape and band
normalization. The physical amplitude, not the OU-prior scale, controls this
distortion term.
